   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<br><br><br>I am using ggplot2 to prepare some plots, and I noticed some errors when using geom_bar() with facet_wrap().<br><br>I attached the file &quot;example.list&quot; if you want to reproduce the problem.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">R<br><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gridExtra</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;example.list&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">h</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df$V1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scale_x_discrete</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">limits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;boat&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bike&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;car&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">facet_wrap</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> V2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scales </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;free_y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ggsave</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;plots_facet_wrap.pdf&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br>=&gt; This will produce a plot with problem, because I should have 28 yellow boats, bu the plot clearly shows below 25.<br><br><br>If I produce three separate plots by separating the colours, everything works fine:<br><br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">green_type  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subset</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df$V2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;green&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>red_type    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subset</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df$V2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>yellow_type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subset</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df$V2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;yellow&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">green_type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">green_type$V1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scale_x_discrete</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">limits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;boat&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bike&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;car&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">red_type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">red_type$V1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scale_x_discrete</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">limits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;boat&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bike&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;car&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p3 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yellow_type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yellow_type$V1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scale_x_discrete</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">limits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;boat&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bike&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;car&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>pdf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;plots_no_facet_wrap.pdf&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>grid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">arrange</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>dev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">off</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br>=&gt; 28 yellow boats in the plot, as expected.<br><br><br>Any idea of what is wrong here? Is it my fault or a bug in ggplot2?<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "y2b60bICLagJ",
   "from": "Ron Crump",
   "author": "942ffec526d6a312",
   "date": "2014-11-04T08:46:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unexpected results with bar_plot() and facet_wrap()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "&gt; Any idea of what is wrong here? Is it my fault or a bug in ggplot2?\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "It seems to be to do with the factor(df$V1).\r<br>\r<br>Either of these work for me (number of yellow boats look right and they \r<br>are ordered\r<br>boat, bike, car on the x-axis as per your example):\r<br>\r<br>ggplot(df,aes(x=V1))+geom_bar()+scale_x_discrete(limits=c(&quot;boat&quot;,&quot;bike&quot;,&quot;car&quot;))+facet_wrap(~V2,ncol=1,scales=&quot;free_y&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>ggplot(df,aes(x=factor(V1,levels=c(&quot;boat&quot;,&quot;bike&quot;,&quot;car&quot;))))+geom_bar()+facet_wrap(~V2,ncol=1,scales=&quot;free_y&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>So don&#39;t specify the &quot;df$&quot; in the factor call. It is redundant having \r<br>told ggplot that\r<br>your data are in df already. I don&#39;t know what impact this is then \r<br>having, maybe ggplot\r<br>is working with an internal (in some way reordered) copy of df and your \r<br>specification of\r<br>df$V1 is then wrongly addressing this back to the original. Somebody \r<br>else can probably\r<br>clarify what is going on there.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>Ron.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "yCVgRq2jEMUJ",
   "from": "rst...@ebi.ac.uk",
   "author": "3c31e30148c11e5b",
   "date": "2014-11-04T10:14:22Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unexpected results with bar_plot() and facet_wrap()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Ron.<br><br><br>Thank you very much, removing the &quot;df$&quot; fixed the problem.<br>I am very surprised it is making a difference, since this is the same dataset.<br><br><br>Best regards,<br>Romain</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><br><br>On Tuesday, 4 November 2014 08:46:28 UTC, Ron Crump  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi,\n<br>&gt; Any idea of what is wrong here? Is it my fault or a bug in ggplot2?\n<br>It seems to be to do with the factor(df$V1).\n<br>\n<br>Either of these work for me (number of yellow boats look right and they \n<br>are ordered\n<br>boat, bike, car on the x-axis as per your example):\n<br>\n<br>ggplot(df,aes(x=V1))+geom_bar()+scale_x_discrete(limits=c(&quot;boat&quot;,&quot;bike&quot;,&quot;car&quot;))+facet_wrap(~V2,ncol=1,scales=&quot;free_y&quot;)\n<br>\n<br>ggplot(df,aes(x=factor(V1,levels=c(&quot;boat&quot;,&quot;bike&quot;,&quot;car&quot;))))+geom_bar()+facet_wrap(~V2,ncol=1,scales=&quot;free_y&quot;)\n<br>\n<br>So don&#39;t specify the &quot;df$&quot; in the factor call. It is redundant having \n<br>told ggplot that\n<br>your data are in df already. I don&#39;t know what impact this is then \n<br>having, maybe ggplot\n<br>is working with an internal (in some way reordered) copy of df and your \n<br>specification of\n<br>df$V1 is then wrongly addressing this back to the original. Somebody \n<br>else can probably\n<br>clarify what is going on there.\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>Ron.\n<br></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
